     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Two new letters and one that stays silent",
     "texto": [
      "Spanish has two letters that English doesn't use:\n\n- **la eñe (ñ)**: it sounds like «ny»\n- **la jota (j)**: it sounds like a breathed h, rougher\n\nAnd one letter that exists but never sounds: **la hache (h)**. That's why «hola» is pronounced «ola»."
